atment, to participate in or refuse to participate in experimental research, and to formulate an advance directive.","category":"Resident Rights Deficiencies","concept":"resident_rights","concept_label":"Resident rights & abuse/neglect"},"cms-f0582":{"code":"F-0582","title":"Give residents notice of Medicaid/Medicare coverage and potential liability for services not covered.","category":"Resident Rights Deficiencies","concept":"resident_rights","concept_label":"Resident rights & abuse/neglect"},"cms-f0677":{"code":"F-0677","title":"Provide care and assistance to perform activities of daily living for any resident who is unable.","category":"Quality of Life and Care Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0838":{"code":"F-0838","title":"Conduct and document a facility-wide assessment to determine what resources are necessary to care for residents competently during both day-to-day operations (including nights and weekends) and emergencies.","category":"Administration Deficiencies","concept":"administration","concept_label":"Administration & records"},"cms-f0609":{"code":"F-0609","title":"Timely report suspected abuse, neglect, or theft and report the results of the investigation to proper authorities.","category":"Freedom from Abuse, Neglect, and Exploitation Deficiencies","concept":"resident_rights","concept_label":"Resident rights & abuse/neglect"},"cms-f0627":{"code":"F-0627","title":"Ensure the transfer/discharge meets the resident's needs/preferences and that the resident is prepared for a safe transfer/discharge.","category":"Resident Rights Deficiencies","concept":"resident_rights","concept_label":"Resident rights & abuse/neglect"},"cms-f0761":{"code":"F-0761","title":"Ensure drugs and biologicals used in the facility are labeled in accordance with currently accepted professional principles; and all drugs and biologicals must be stored in locked compartments, separately locked, compartments for controlled drugs.","category":"Pharmacy Service Deficiencies","concept":"medication","concept_label":"Medication management"},"cms-f0622":{"code":"F-0622","title":"Not transfer or discharge a resident without an adequate reason; and must provide documentation and convey specific information  when a resident is transferred or discharged.","category":"Resident Rights Deficiencies","concept":"resident_rights","concept_label":"Resident rights & abuse/neglect"},"cms-f0624":{"code":"F-0624","title":"Prepare residents for a safe transfer or discharge from the nursing home.","category":"Resident Rights Deficiencies","concept":"resident_rights","concept_label":"Resident rights & abuse/neglect"},"cms-f0552":{"code":"F-0552","title":"Ensure that residents are fully informed and understand their health status, care and treatments.","category":"Resident Rights Deficiencies","concept":"resident_rights","concept_label":"Resident rights & abuse/neglect"},"cms-k0521":{"code":"K-0521","title":"Ensure heating and ventilation systems that have been properly installed according to the manufacturer's instructions.","category":"Services Deficiencies","concept":"environment_life_safety","concept_label":"Environment & life safety"},"cms-k0918":{"code":"K-0918","title":"Have generator or other power source capable of supplying service within 10 seconds.","category":"Gas, Vacuum, and Electrical Systems Deficiencies","concept":"environment_life_safety","concept_label":"Environment & life safety"},"cms-k0345":{"code":"K-0345","title":"Have approved installation, maintenance and testing program for fire alarm systems.","category":"Smoke Deficiencies","concept":"environment_life_safety","concept_label":"Environment & life safety"},"cms-k0920":{"code":"K-0920","title":"Ensure proper usage of power strips and extension cords.","category":"Gas, Vacuum, and Electrical Systems Deficiencies","concept":"environment_life_safety","concept_label":"Environment & life safety"},"cms-f0554":{"code":"F-0554","title":"Allow residents to s